          "description": "Living in Bondage: Breaking Free (2019), directed by Ramsey Nouah and starring Jide Kene Achufusi, Ramsey Nouah, and Kenneth Okonkwo, is a Nigerian drama with supernatural elements. The story follows an ambitious young man whose meteoric rise, guided by a mysterious tycoon, becomes entangled with a secret occult brotherhood and escalating moral compromises. The film foregrounds themes of materialism, power, corruption, and the spiritual cost of ambition, presented through glossy production design and tense, atmospheric cinematography. Its emotional tone is tense and unsettling, balancing spectacle with intimate character drama.",
